---
title: Customizing Invoice PDFs
description: Make your invoice PDFs match your brand with custom CSS and HTML templates.
---

FOSSBilling generates invoice PDFs with [Dompdf](https://github.com/dompdf/dompdf), which renders HTML and CSS into a printable document.

## Create an Override

In `modules/Invoice/templates/pdf/`, copy the default file for the change you want to make.

| To Change | Copy | Save As |
|-----------|------|---------|
| Styling | `default-invoice.css` | `custom-invoice.css` |
| HTML structure | `default-invoice.twig` | `custom-invoice.twig` |

FOSSBilling uses your custom files automatically. Edit those copies because updates replace the default files.

## Logos and Remote Assets

Dompdf cannot fetch remote assets directly. Custom PDF templates must use local or embedded images, styles, and fonts. Use the supplied `logo_source` variable for the company logo and `css` for the invoice stylesheet instead of adding remote URLs.

FOSSBilling fetches remote company logos separately, blocking private networks and checking image types, contents, and dimensions. Downloads are limited to 2 MiB, and SVG logos must be self-contained. Unavailable or rejected remote logos are omitted from the PDF.

If a logo is missing, check that it is publicly reachable, uses a supported image format (PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, WebP, or self-contained SVG), and meets the size limits. Internal-only logo services cannot be used as remote sources. Generate a test PDF after changing the logo or custom assets.

## CSS Limitations

Use basic positioning and table layouts. Avoid flexbox and grid, and keep each table row short enough to fit on one page. See [Dompdf's CSS compatibility reference](https://github.com/dompdf/dompdf/wiki/CSSCompatibility) for supported properties.

## CSS Classes Reference

![PDF layout with CSS classes](../../../assets/invoice-layout.png)

The default stylesheet uses these classes:

- `.CompanyLogo` — Company logo image
- `.TopSectionDivider` — Divider below the header area
- `.InvoiceInfo` — Invoice number, dates, and status
- `.CompanyInfo` — Seller/company heading and details
- `.ClientInfo` — Client heading and details
- `.Breakdown` — Line items, tax, discount, and total table
- `.InvoiceText` — Custom invoice text blocks
- `.InvoiceFooter` — Payment details, company footer, and signature
- `.muted-text` — Muted footer signature text

## Custom HTML Template

### Template Variables

Use these variables in `custom-invoice.twig`.

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `currency_code` | Invoice currency code for `format_currency`. |
| `css` | Contents of `custom-invoice.css` or `default-invoice.css`, inserted into the template's `<style>` block. |
| `logo_source` | Resolved company logo source: a local path, an image data URI (including validated remote logos), or an empty string. Dompdf does not fetch remote URLs. |
| `seller` | Display-ready seller/company lines keyed by labels such as `Name`, `Address 1`, `Phone`, and `VAT Number`. |
| `seller_lines` | Number of seller lines used by the default template for layout calculations. |
| `footer` | Company footer details, including company name, bank details, address fields, email, phone, VAT/company number, website, and signature. |
| `buyer` | Display-ready buyer/client lines keyed by labels such as `Company`, `Name`, `Address`, `City`, `Country`, `Phone`, and `VAT Number`. |
| `buyer_lines` | Number of buyer lines used by the default template for layout calculations. |
| `invoice` | Full invoice API array. Line items are in `invoice.lines`; raw buyer, seller, and client data are in `invoice.buyer`, `invoice.seller`, and `invoice.client`. |

The PDF renderer does not provide top-level `client`, `company`, or `currency` variables. Use `invoice.client`, `seller`/`footer`, and `currency_code` instead.

### Example: Add a Custom Header

```twig {% process=false %}
<div class="custom-header">
  {% if logo_source %}
  <img src="{{ logo_source }}" alt="{{ seller['Name']|default(seller['Company']|default('Company logo'|trans)) }}">
  {% endif %}
  <h1>{{ 'Invoice'|trans }} #{{ invoice.serie_nr }}</h1>
</div>
```

### Twig Filters

PDF templates support the same [Twig filters](/extensions-and-development/twig-filters/) available elsewhere in FOSSBilling:

```twig
{{ invoice.total|format_currency(currency_code) }}  {# Format as currency #}
{{ invoice.created_at|format_date }}                {# Format the invoice date #}
{{ invoice.text_1|default('')|markdown_to_html }}   {# Render invoice text as HTML #}
```

## Testing Changes

{% steps %}
1. Make your edits to `custom-invoice.css` or `custom-invoice.twig`
2. Generate a test invoice
3. Download the PDF
4. Review the output
{% /steps %}

{% aside type="tip" %}
If your Twig template changes do not appear, [clear the application cache](/maintenance/troubleshooting/#clearing-the-cache).
{% /aside %}

## Debugging

For complex issues, enable FOSSBilling debug mode in `config.php`:

```php
'debug_and_monitoring' => [
    'debug' => true,
],
```

Then review your PHP or FOSSBilling logs for Dompdf-related messages.
